---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `Six of us go out and I always end up doing the math.
Bill, tip percent, how many people. Tell me what each
person owes. And round it up, nobody wants to hand over
four point one six pounds.`;

const SampleOutput = `Bill: 98.40  Tip: 18%  People: 6
Each person owes: $19.36
Collected: $116.16  (bill + tip was $116.11)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-5" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 5
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Tip Split</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code code={Brief} frame="code" lang="txt" title="What they asked for" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-5">Set 5</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Three parameters. Decide their order and write it in your requirements list &mdash; you will get it wrong once otherwise.</li>
            <li>Rounding <i>up</i> is not the same as rounding. Look up how to do it, or work out the trick with what you know.</li>
            <li>If the rounded amounts add up to more than the bill, that is correct and worth mentioning in your output.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code code={SampleOutput} frame="terminal" title="Sample Output" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">Rounding <i>up</i> gives 19.36 and collects 5 cents more than the bill. Round to nearest and you collect a penny short. Say which you chose and why.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-tip-split</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
